Camille, Gretchen,<br />
<br />
Read this. It is Marchwood's chief compliance officer, in writing, to our e=
xaminer, two days before we closed. I am quoting it exactly.<br />
<br />
"Marchwood accepts Item 4. Effective June 1, 2011 all 214 affected client a=
ccounts have been transferred to Signal Peak Trust Company, a qualified cus=
todian unaffiliated with Marchwood, under custodial agreements that give Ma=
rchwood no authority to withdraw funds or securities. We have discontinued =
the direct fee-debit instruction described in Item 4 firm-wide. We will not=
 resume it."<br />
<br />
And then:<br />
<br />
"Marchwood further undertakes to apply this same treatment to any advisory =
accounts it acquires or onboards in the future, and to obtain the surprise =
examination required by Rule 206(4)-2(a)(4) by an independent public accoun=
tant, with the corresponding Form ADV-E filing, for any period in which Mar=
chwood is deemed to have custody of client funds or securities. This undert=
aking is not limited to calendar year 2010 or to any other period and is gi=
ven without an expiration date."<br />
<br />
And the last line, which is the one I would put on the first page of the op=
position:<br />
<br />
"Please treat this letter as the corrective action commitment on which the =
staff's closing of examination 2011-0447 is conditioned."<br />
<br />
The motion says nothing was required of Marchwood in 2011. Marchwood's own =
compliance officer wrote to us that everything was required of it, describe=
d what it had already done, and asked us to close on that basis. Our closin=
g letter of June 28 is not a clearance. It is the acceptance of this letter=
, which is exactly what it says on its face - "based on the corrective acti=
ons described in your response."<br />
<br />
